   "fen": "rnbq1rk1/ppp1ppbp/3p1np1/8/3PPP2/2NB1N2/PPP3PP/R1BQK2R b KQ - 4 6",
   "line": [
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Bc4 would be the natural-looking mistake — it runs into Nxe4 and d5, blasting the centre apart. So the bishop goes to d3 instead, quietly buttressing e4. Not every piece has to climb Everest.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Place a piece to defend your centre even if the square looks passive; the flashy square can hang tactically."
